===Verb===
{{en-verb|++}} {{lb|en|originally|US}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[supply#Verb|supply]] (a [[device]], [[structure#Noun|structure]], etc.) with [[new#Adjective|new]] [[component#Noun|components]] or [[part#Noun|parts]] that were not [[previously]] [[available]] or [[install#Verb|installed]]; to [[modernize]].
##: {{synonyms|en|backfit}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=Richard Clinnick|title=Midlands Metro Welcomes New Catenary-free Trams|magazine=[[w:Rail (magazine)|Rail]]|location=Peterborough, Cambridgeshire|publisher=[[w:Bauer Media Group|Bauer Media]]|date=2 January 2020|page=16|issn=0953-4563|oclc=999467860|passage=Trams dating from 2012 have been '''retro-fitted''' with lithium batteries, with the conversions starting in 2018.}}
## To [[add#Verb|add]] or [[substitute#Verb|substitute]] (new components or parts) that were not previously available for or installed in a device, structure, etc.
##: {{synonyms|en|backfit}}
## {{lb|en|computing}} {{synonym of|en|backport|t=to [[retroactively]] supply a [[fix#Noun|fix]] or [[feature]] to a previous [[version#Noun|version]] of a [[software]] product at the same time or after supplying it to the current version.}}
##: {{ux|en|The bug was so bad that we had to '''retrofit''' our patch to the last three releases, as well as the newest release.}}
## {{lb|en|figuratively}} To [[give#Verb|give]] new [[characteristic#Noun|characteristics]] or [[make#Verb|make]] [[alteration]]s (to someone or something) to [[suit#Verb|suit]] them to [[changed#Adjective|changed]] [[circumstance#Noun|circumstances]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To supply a device, structure, etc., with new components or parts that were not previously available or installed.

